{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Active Object in Python.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Active Object in Python.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender active object in python blender active object in python","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Active Object in Python.md","fileName":"Blender Active Object in Python.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Active Object in Python","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Python Data and Operations]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Python Data and Operations","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Active Object in Python.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Active Object in Python.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender active object in python blender active object in python","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Active Object in Python.md","fileName":"Blender Active Object in Python.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Active Object in Python","heading":"Blender Active Object in Python","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The active object is the single object Blender treats as the primary target in the current context. It may be read from context and is often the object whose properties, mode, or mesh data an operator uses.\n\nActivation does not mean the same thing as selection. Several objects can be selected while only one is active, and changing the active object can alter the result of the same context-sensitive call. A robust script establishes both the selected set and the active member before relying on an operator.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Python Data and Operations","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":